    "content": "The Augusta National course record during the Masters Tournament is a 9-under-par 63, held by Nick Price (1986, third round) and Greg Norman (1996, first round). It is considered one of the most enduring records in golf, standing for 40 years.Lowest Tournament Score: 63 (Nick Price, 1986; Greg Norman, 1996).Near Misses: Several players have recorded 64, including Lloyd Mangrum (1940), Jordan Spieth (2015, 2018), and Rory McIlroy (2022).Member's Course Record: According to reports, long-time member and former Masters non-playing marker Jeff Knox holds the club record of 61 from the members' tees.The 63 remains the lowest score in tournament history, with the record remaining untouched since 1996.",
